  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because the roots are \\(m,\\) \\(n,\\) Vieta gives \\(m+n=-m\\) and \\(mn=n.\\) Since \\(n\\ne0,\\) the second equation gives \\(m=1,\\) and then \\(n=-2.\\) Their sum is \\(-1.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Use both the sum and product forms of Vieta’s formulas",
        "The product equation and \\(n\\ne0\\) determine \\(m\\)"
      ],
